      "value": "@{60285ca04963ba22994f485b|full_name} \n\nEven tho the feature is set still as \" available in future release \" after all this time and hasnt been closed. I thought its best to ask it here since its related.\n\nHope its alright to respond in here about this. The other day was messing around with the \"snap to hand\" feature turned on. and and \"grab movement\" set to 1. Had a phys bone set on avatar 1 Attached either in the Root or in the Armature. And another person in an avatar would try to grab it. Expecting it to follow it in rotation locked state due to \" snap to hand \".\n\nBut instead it behaves like the Y axis is being refrenced from the Phys bone chain instaed of the hand. And that snap to hand only does 2 Axis (X and Z in this instance) locking to the hand. So it wouldnt rotation lock to the hand in all axis. Wich would lead to if the sharing objects from avatars with the \"snap to hand feature \" to not snap correctly. so be it a phone or a Handle rotating in respective to the avatar its from. If they move. It would influence the Y rotation still while the other person holds on to it.\n\nHere my questions are that \n\n1. this behaviour the expected behaviour intended out of curiostiy?\n\n2. is it possible to add an extra override toggle switch that would let you snap the Y axis Rotation to the hand aswell?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-03T08:13:58.802Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "- PhysBones have been adjusted to use and maintain the initial hand-to-bone offset** as your \"grab position\" instead of a fixed relative position per bone. This means that grabbed PhysBones won't move or \"snap\" when you initially grab. They will only move when you move the grabbing hand.\n\nPlease allow creators to disable this functionality on a per physbone basis. While it is great for hair or other natural uses of physbones, some technical uses of physbones are negatively impacted by this change. For example, some systems use physbones to snap objects to you or other peoples hands adding interactivity to props. Avatars that use physbones to measure how far a object is pulled (one example would be like a rip cord on a chainsaw prop, or a handle on a transforming scythe) will no longer be accurate and will no longer place the hand in a good position. \n\nPlease consider giving us this option.",
